s read a lot of history and  and I see these struggles have been  going on all through human history you  know I go back to the ancient Greeks and  the Greek city-states Athens Sparta  Thebes Corinth each one of them having  struggles between the Oleg arcs on one  hand and the Democrats on the other hand  and it's it's always just to struggle  between the the rich and the powerful on  one hand and the rest of the population  on the other hand someone asked me in an  interview the other day about science  fiction and why science fiction is less  popular than it once was obviously and  fantasy has become much more popular and  I think it's because the at least of the  United States and possibly here and in  Europe as well a lot of people have lost  faith in the future which science  fiction represented and the great dream  of space travel of that we would go to  the moon and we would have bases on the  moon and we would go to Mars and  eventually humanity would spread out  among the stars and all of that no one  seems to really believe that anymore and  it doesn't seem to be the the real faith  that our children will have it better  than we have it and their children will  have it better than they have it instead  there's just a reversed as these worries  about global warming and  the worries about pollution of the  ecosphere  you know peak oil energy running out  where the where the renewable energy  resources to replace it how long can  this industrial civilization last if  energy does will run out answer by the  way  not long so where is this all gonna put  us I you know I don't know but it does  it does depress me when I think about it  I I think all we can do you know as a  writer I write my books and I  occasionally influence people with  statements on my blog perhaps but I  think ultimately it's up to the people  of each individual country and my  country in particular being the last  superpower in the world and exercising a  frighteningly disproportion  disproportionate amount of power over  the world to try to address some of  these problems and I think particularly  it falls on the younger people in this  audience I hope you guys are doing  something about it and my generation you  know when I was one of these proverbial  younger people I was out there trying to  get us out of Vietnam and you know a  part of movements the first Earth Day  the ecology movement all of these things  to try to produce a better world and we  had some victories and we had some of  the feats I think by and large we made  the world a better place than we left it  but that doesn't mean that utopia ensued  and utopia will never ensue it has to be  fought for again with each generation  and if it's not fought for if people  just let the vampires rule then I gotta  warn you winter is coming  [Applause]
 

